* `AGENT_RUNTIME_KEY` — the worker authenticates to OWEN's own `/api/crm-link/events` adapter
  with it. It must be a live OWEN API key holding **`agent_write`**. Without it, events are
  not queued at all and you get a WARNING saying so (rather than five failed deliveries).
* `OWEN_INTERNAL_URL` — already defaults to `http://app:8888`, which is correct.

**Per-number configuration is DATA, in `crm_links`** — no deploy to change it:

```
python -m app.integrations.crm.manage list
python -m app.integrations.crm.manage bind --phone +1XXXXXXXXXX \
    --pstn +1YYYYYYYYYY --pstn +1ZZZZZZZZZZ \
    --operator you@dreamteamroofingfl.com --outbound-operator you@dreamteamroofingfl.com
python -m app.integrations.crm.manage enable  --phone +1XXXXXXXXXX
python -m app.integrations.crm.manage disable --phone +1XXXXXXXXXX
python -m app.integrations.crm.manage unbind  --phone +1XXXXXXXXXX
```

`--operator` may be repeated, or omitted entirely to ring **every operator whose softphone is
currently registered** (the presence rule the platform already uses).

